00:18:36,966 --> 00:18:42,191
[SPEAKER_00]: And how to maintain the vertical view and not to run away and hide in distractions?

243
00:18:42,251 --> 00:18:42,511
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

244
00:18:42,791 --> 00:18:48,336
[SPEAKER_00]: How do you, as a monk, as someone who's practicing, how do you...?

245
00:18:48,376 --> 00:18:51,980
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, by developing mindfulness in your day life,

246
00:18:52,990 --> 00:19:02,893
[SPEAKER_01]: Not mindfulness in terms of some kind of weird robotic method, meditation, repetition, noting, but mindfulness in the sense of recognizing intentions behind your actions.

247
00:19:03,293 --> 00:19:08,334
[SPEAKER_01]: Because for as long as you perform a certain action, intention to do that action is there, on a more general level.

248
00:19:08,854 --> 00:19:12,776
[SPEAKER_01]: So you're mindful of the reasons why you're doing things, why you want to do things.

249
00:19:13,356 --> 00:19:16,577
[SPEAKER_01]: And if they're utterly unwholesome, you don't do it.

250
00:19:16,717 --> 00:19:21,578
[SPEAKER_01]: If it's something you have to do, then you reroute it into something that's not unwholesome.

251
00:19:24,197 --> 00:19:29,922
[SPEAKER_01]: Such as eating food, as we discussed before, can be rooted in a very unwholesome, pure sensuality.

252
00:19:30,763 --> 00:19:37,929
[SPEAKER_01]: Or, if you contemplate and dwell on it and drill it long enough, you can root it in, no, I'll root it in necessity and I don't care what I eat.

253
00:19:39,311 --> 00:19:48,039
[SPEAKER_01]: Whether it's, you know, the softest, nicest food or the roughest, because you remain rooted in the necessity of eating food to sustain the body so that you can practice.

254
00:19:50,032 --> 00:20:06,358
[SPEAKER_01]: So, by being aware of your reasons and intentions, you will basically... well, you won't be able to fall into bad faith, you won't be able to fall into that self-deception, and you won't be doing things for the sake of distraction.

255
00:20:09,980 --> 00:20:16,142
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's how the vertical view is maintained, or, well, developed.

256
00:20:16,924 --> 00:20:22,567
[SPEAKER_01]: Because it will take time to kind of elevate your mind to start looking vertically at the nature of things.

257
00:20:22,647 --> 00:20:31,972
[SPEAKER_01]: Because it's been just going, you know, flowing very horizontally with a powerful flow of sensuality and distraction.

258
00:20:32,832 --> 00:20:39,755
[SPEAKER_01]: So that's why, you know, people who don't... well, people who haven't been practicing, but they might get the hint of it.

