472
00:36:34,575 --> 00:36:35,617
[SPEAKER_01]: It would have been rooted in...

473
00:36:35,817 --> 00:36:39,763
[SPEAKER_01]: There's nothing unwholesome with sitting down once you've been walking.

474
00:36:40,544 --> 00:36:45,191
[SPEAKER_01]: But if you're doing it for the reasons of fear that arose while you were walking, that is unwholesome.

475
00:36:46,032 --> 00:36:47,814
[SPEAKER_01]: And nobody externally can tell you that.

476
00:36:48,215 --> 00:36:49,595
[SPEAKER_01]: Because nobody externally can see that.

477
00:36:50,216 --> 00:36:55,077
[SPEAKER_01]: Which is why, don't pay much heed to people judging things based on external factors.

478
00:36:55,657 --> 00:36:57,377
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, and there's another situation.

479
00:36:57,397 --> 00:37:06,360
[SPEAKER_01]: There's, you know, monks, or people who are very agreeable, very soft-spoken, and people love them, and people praise them, and it's so great, it's so nice, companions, and they're completely ignorant to two things.

480
00:37:06,840 --> 00:37:14,642
[SPEAKER_01]: And then you had other people, who were, or monks and people, who were quite hard to live with, unbearable, rude, whatever else, and there were islands.

481
00:37:16,950 --> 00:37:20,754
[SPEAKER_01]: Because those things pertain basically to personal levels.

482
00:37:21,235 --> 00:37:23,797
[SPEAKER_01]: So, as you can see, oh, no, he sat down because he was tired.

483
00:37:24,358 --> 00:37:27,161
[SPEAKER_01]: That's what externally might appear like.

484
00:37:27,922 --> 00:37:30,104
[SPEAKER_01]: But no, he sat down because he was afraid of walking.

