00:37:38,905 --> 00:37:39,145
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

488
00:37:39,245 --> 00:37:40,786
[SPEAKER_01]: And he didn't want them to waste the food.

489
00:37:40,906 --> 00:37:41,066
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

490
00:37:41,086 --> 00:37:41,886
[SPEAKER_01]: They would be starving.

491
00:37:42,066 --> 00:37:44,788
[SPEAKER_00]: But there's some, some people would say, oh, what kind of monk is that?

492
00:37:44,808 --> 00:37:47,969
[SPEAKER_00]: He doesn't, doesn't keep that rule and stores food.

493
00:37:47,989 --> 00:37:48,089
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

494
00:37:48,129 --> 00:37:58,094
[SPEAKER_01]: The Buddha did remind him, but not on that personal level, but just on a, from a, from a, like a, like a higher perspective point of view, whereby in the future, doing that,

495
00:37:58,914 --> 00:38:04,498
[SPEAKER_01]: will most likely result in unwholesome, because most people are not actually developed as that monk.

496
