00:38:27,425 --> 00:38:30,226
[SPEAKER_00]: It's not a measure of somebody's attainment.

501
00:38:30,246 --> 00:38:30,486
[SPEAKER_00]: No.

502
00:38:30,766 --> 00:38:33,427
[SPEAKER_00]: If he gets blamed or praised... Not at all.

503
00:38:33,447 --> 00:38:36,008
[SPEAKER_00]: ...it's going to be on the level of... ...of Kutujan.

504
00:38:36,028 --> 00:38:36,968
[SPEAKER_01]: ...of the ludhidus.

505
00:38:37,028 --> 00:38:38,269
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if they praise you...

506
00:38:38,469 --> 00:38:41,230
[SPEAKER_01]: If Kutujan praises an arahant, he does it for the wrong reasons.

507
00:38:41,550 --> 00:38:44,731
[SPEAKER_01]: Because if he were to do it for the right reasons, he would be at least Sotāpanna himself.

508
00:38:45,031 --> 00:38:46,231
[SPEAKER_01]: He would know where the right reasons are.

509
00:38:46,351 --> 00:38:47,072
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

510
00:38:47,112 --> 00:38:50,293
[SPEAKER_01]: If Kutujan blames the arahant, again, he does it for the wrong reasons.

511
00:38:51,773 --> 00:38:52,893
[SPEAKER_01]: Because if he were to have the right

512
00:39:00,323 --> 00:39:15,231
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, you know, people just assume, like, you need to have... well, based on your own, you know, life and learning or whatever, you just assume that a wise person, person knows must be some, you know, old man,

513
00:39:17,455 --> 00:39:20,496
[SPEAKER_01]: But then you have in the suttas, you have like... How was that?

514
00:39:20,777 --> 00:39:21,917
[SPEAKER_01]: When the king came to the...

515
00:39:21,957 --> 00:39:25,298
[SPEAKER_01]: The widow was staying in the forest grove, sort of.

516
00:39:25,918 --> 00:39:27,739
[SPEAKER_01]: And the king went to see him.

517
00:39:28,319 --> 00:39:29,660
[SPEAKER_01]: I think King Pasenadi, maybe.

518
00:39:30,620 --> 00:39:35,242
[SPEAKER_01]: And on the way there, he was meeting all these monks, doing walking meditation and just living there.

519
00:39:35,662 --> 00:39:40,644
[SPEAKER_01]: And they were all, like, young, in the prime of their youth life.

520
00:39:40,844 --> 00:39:43,545
[SPEAKER_01]: They could still fully enjoy sensual pleasures.

521
00:39:44,625 --> 00:39:46,386
[SPEAKER_01]: And they look really happy and healthy.

522
00:39:47,316 --> 00:39:48,737
[SPEAKER_01]: In this remote forest.

523
00:39:49,417 --> 00:39:52,318
[SPEAKER_01]: And then he went to the Buddha, and he was just smitten by this whole thing.

524
00:39:52,338 --> 00:39:54,139
[SPEAKER_01]: It was just such an experience.

525
00:39:54,859 --> 00:40:01,322
[SPEAKER_01]: He was praising it, and he said, yeah, because, you know, they don't follow an account of any external observances, and there's something like an account of those things.

526
00:40:01,702 --> 00:40:03,002
[SPEAKER_01]: They follow because they understood the dhamma.

527
00:40:03,583 --> 00:40:04,523
[SPEAKER_01]: And, you know, what?

528
00:40:04,543 --> 00:40:06,344
[SPEAKER_01]: You had children, back in the day.

529
00:40:07,224 --> 00:40:11,868
[SPEAKER_01]: Understanding the dhamma, obviously, that's quite unlikely today, but it's still possible.

530
00:40:12,629 --> 00:40:19,054
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's this understanding which can't be really measured externally, certainly not by the measure of patujan.

531
00:40:20,456 --> 00:40:21,296
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's quite...

532
00:40:21,396 --> 00:40:27,542
[SPEAKER_01]: I think that's also a useful thing for somebody who knows that he's a patujan and wants to practice to know, because

